CacheName -- determines hash table in which to cache solutions to the deformation equation
******************************************************************************************

Description
===========

CacheName is the name of an optional argument, whose value is either a *note
mutable hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, or *note null:
(Macaulay2Doc)null,. After each stage of lifting, the methods *note
versalDeformation: versalDeformation, and *note localHilbertScheme:
localHilbertScheme, will store the solution to the deformation equation in
CacheName#VersalDeformationResults. If the value of CacheName is *note null:
(Macaulay2Doc)null, as is the default, then the solution is stored in the hash
table described in the documentation of *note versalDeformation:
versalDeformation, and *note localHilbertScheme: localHilbertScheme,.

Functions with optional argument named CacheName:
=================================================

  * "versalDeformation(List,List,List,List,CacheName=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(Matrix,CacheName=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix,CacheName=>...)"
  * "localHilbertScheme(...,CacheName=>...)" -- see *note localHilbertScheme:
    localHilbertScheme, -- computes a power series representation of the local
    Hilbert scheme

