correctDeformation -- correct lifting to avoid obstructions at next order
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (F,R) = correctDeformation(f,r,g,c)
        (F,R) = correctDeformation(S,M,L)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * r, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * g, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * (f,r,g,c), a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * SanityCheck => ..., default value true
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value 0, control the verbosity
        of output
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices
      * R, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices

Description
===========

Each element of the sequence (F,R) is a list of matrices in increasing powers
of the deformation parameter. (f,r,g,c) should be as in the output of *note
liftDeformation: liftDeformation, and (M,L)should be as in the output of *note
correctionMatrix: correctionMatrix,. If the latter are omitted, they are
replaced by (M,L)=correctionMatrix(f_1,r_1).

correctDeformation perturbs the last entries of f and r such that if possible,
the next invocation of *note liftDeformation: liftDeformation, will introduce
no new terms in the obstruction equations.  If *note SanityCheck: SanityCheck,
is set to *note true: (Macaulay2Doc)true,, as is the default, then the
algorithm will check that the corrected perturbation really does solve the
deformation equation, and terminate with an error if this is not the case.

For example, consider a degenerate twisted cubic curve, see *note [PS85]: Top,:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x,y,z,w];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F0=matrix {{x*z,y*z,z^2,x^3}};                                          |
|                                                                             |
|             1      4                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (f,r,g,c)=localHilbertScheme(F0,Verbose=>0,HighestOrder=>2,SmartLift=>  |
|Warning: calculation terminated since HighestOrder has been reached.         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|false);                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (liftDeformation(f,r,g,c))_2                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {| t_1t_16             |, | 0                                     |}    |
|      | t_9t_16             |  | -2t_6t_10t_16+3t_10^2t_16-t_8t_11t_16 |     |
|      | -t_4t_16            |  | t_8t_10t_16+2t_3t_11t_16              |     |
|      | -2t_14t_16+t_15t_16 |  | 4t_10t_12t_16+2t_11t_13t_16-t_8t_16^2 |     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (F,R)=correctDeformation(f,r,g,c);                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : (liftDeformation(F,R,g,c))_2                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {| t_1t_16             |, 0}                                            |
|      | t_9t_16             |                                                |
|      | -t_4t_16            |                                                |
|      | -2t_14t_16+t_15t_16 |                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

If the obstruction space is zero, this will generate an error.

Ways to use correctDeformation:
===============================

  * "correctDeformation(List,List,List,List)"
  * "correctDeformation(Sequence,Matrix,List)"

