CorrectionMatrix -- determines the first order deformations used in correcting liftings
***************************************************************************************

Description
===========

CorrectionMatrix is the name of an optional argument, whose value is either a
*note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, with value auto or a *note sequence:
(Macaulay2Doc)Sequence, of the form output by *note correctionMatrix:
correctionMatrix,. The second term in the sequence is a list of two matrices
which give some parameter-free first-order deformations and the corresponding
lifted relations, respectively. The first term in the sequence is a *note
matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, which describes the action on liftings of
equations by the specified first-order deformations.  If set to auto, *note
correctionMatrix: correctionMatrix, is used to calculate the relevant sequence.
The default value of CorrectionMatrix is auto.

