DegreeBound -- determines the degree limit used to compute the tangent cone of obstruction equations
****************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

DegreeBound is the name of an optional argument. Its value is an *note integer:
(Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or infinity. When lifting a deformation, the tangent cone for
the obstruction equations is computed using a local term order. The computation
uses the command *note gb: (Macaulay2Doc)gb, with the option *note DegreeLimit:
(Macaulay2Doc)DegreeLimit, set to the order to which the deformation has been
lifted, plus DegreeBound. Default value is 0. If *note SanityCheck:
SanityCheck, is set to true and results in an error being returned, this can be
corrected by re-running the computation using a higher value of DegreeBound.

Functions with optional argument named DegreeBound:
===================================================

  * "liftDeformation(...,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "localHilbertScheme(...,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "nestedHilbertScheme(...,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "nestedVersalDeformation(...,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(List,List,List,List,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(Matrix,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix,DegreeBound=>...)"
  * "versalDeformation(NestedDeformation,DegreeBound=>...)"

