extMatrix -- calculate obstruction space for modules
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = extMatrix(F) 
        N = extMatrix(deg,F) 
        N = extMatrix(lo,hi,F)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * deg, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, or *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * lo, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or -*note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,
      * hi, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * SourceRing => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,

Description
===========

The output N is a matrix over the same ring as F whose columns form a basis for
(a graded piece of) the first extension module Ext^1(image F,coker F).
Selection of graded pieces is done in the same manner as with *note basis:
(Macaulay2Doc)basis,. If the selected pieces are infinite dimensional, an error
occurs. The optional argument *note SourceRing: (Macaulay2Doc)SourceRing, may
be used in the same fashion as with *note basis: (Macaulay2Doc)basis,.

For example, consider the module M4 over an E6 singularity, see *note [Si01]:
Top,:

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x,y]/ideal {x^4+y^3};               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F= matrix {{y,-x^2,0},{x,0,-y},{0,-y,-x}}|
|                                              |
|o2 = | y -x2 0  |                             |
|     | x 0   -y |                             |
|     | 0 -y  -x |                             |
|                                              |
|             3      3                         |
|o2 : Matrix S  <-- S                          |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N=extMatrix(F)                           |
|                                              |
|o3 = {-4} | 0 0 -x 0 0  -y |                  |
|     {-4} | 1 y 0  0 0  0  |                  |
|     {-4} | 0 0 0  1 y  0  |                  |
|     {-4} | 1 y 0  0 0  x  |                  |
|     {-4} | 0 0 0  1 y  0  |                  |
|     {-4} | 0 0 -1 0 0  0  |                  |
|     {-4} | 0 0 y  x xy 0  |                  |
|     {-4} | 0 0 0  0 0  -y |                  |
|     {-4} | 1 y 0  0 0  0  |                  |
|                                              |
|             9      6                         |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                          |
+----------------------------------------------+

There are six obstructions to deforming this module.

