NestedDeformation -- The class of all nested deformations
*********************************************************

Description
===========

A NestedDeformation is a type of *note MutableHashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, encoding the deformation of a pair consisting
of a scheme  $Y$ and subscheme $X$ or of a module $M_Y$ and quotient module
$M_X$. A NestedDeformation is not typically created by hand, but rather with
the methods *note setupNestedDeformation: setupNestedDeformation,, *note
nestedHilbertScheme: nestedHilbertScheme,, *note nestedVersalDeformation:
nestedVersalDeformation,, *note versalDeformation: versalDeformation,, or *note
liftDeformation: liftDeformation,.

A NestedDeformation has keys "FX" , "RX" , "CX" , "FY" , "RY" , "CY" , "CXY" ,
"G" , "H" , "Xperturb" , "Yperturb" , "T2basis" , "O1" . The values of "FX" ,
"RX" , "G" , "CX" , and "FY" , "RY" , "G" , "CY" ,  are lists of matrices and
respectively encode deformations of $X$ and $Y$ or $M_X$ and $M_Y$ as described
in the documentation node for *note versalDeformation: versalDeformation,. The
values of "CXY" , "H" ,  are also lists of matrices. Taking sums of all lists
involved, one has the additional deformation equation $$ (\mathrm{transpose}\
\mathrm{flatten}\ (FX\cdot H-FY))+CXY\cdot G=0 $$ modulo an appropriate power
of the maximal ideal demonstrating the deformation of $X$ (respectively $M_X$)
as a subscheme (respectively quotient) of the deformation of $Y$ (respectively
$M_Y$).

 The values of "Xperturb" , "Yperturb" , "T2basis" , and "O1"  are for internal
use and may be ignored by the user.

The user may extract the obstruction equations and families of a
NestedDeformation via the methods *note obstructions: obstructions, and *note
families: families,.

See *note nestedHilbertScheme: nestedHilbertScheme, and *note
nestedVersalDeformation: nestedVersalDeformation, for several examples.

Methods that use an object of class NestedDeformation:
======================================================

  * "families(NestedDeformation)" -- see *note families: families, -- outputs
    the perturbed families of a NestedDeformation
  * "isPolynomial(NestedDeformation)" -- see *note isPolynomial: isPolynomial,
    -- checks if a deformation lifts to arbitrary order
  * *note liftDeformation(NestedDeformation):
    liftDeformation_lpNestedDeformation_rp, -- lift a nested deformation to the
    next order
  * "obstructions(NestedDeformation)" -- see *note obstructions: obstructions,
    -- outputs the obstruction equations of a NestedDeformation
  * "sanityCheck(ZZ,NestedDeformation)" -- see *note sanityCheck: sanityCheck,
    -- checks if deformation data satisfies the deformation equation at a
    certain order
  * *note versalDeformation(NestedDeformation):
    versalDeformation_lpNestedDeformation_rp, -- continues calculation of  a
    versal deformation

For the programmer
==================

The object *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note MutableHashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, <
*note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

