sanityCheck -- checks if deformation data satisfies the deformation equation at a certain order
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        B = sanityCheck(n,D) 
        B = sanityCheck(n,L)
        
  * Inputs:
      * n, an element of *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * D, a *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation,
      * L, a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,

Description
===========

The list L should be a list of the form L={F,R,G,C}, where each element is a
list of matrices as output by *note versalDeformation: versalDeformation,. The
integer n must be at most the order of the deformation data.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x,y];                        |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2+y^2);                 |
|                                         |
|o2 : Ideal of S                          |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : (F,R,G,C)=versalDeformation(gens I);|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : sanityCheck(2,{F,R,G,C})            |
|                                         |
|o4 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

