versalDeformation(List,List,List,List) -- continues calculation of  a versal deformation
****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note versalDeformation: versalDeformation,
  * Usage: 
        (F,R,G,C) = versalDeformation(f,r,g,c)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * r, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * g, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CacheName: CacheName, => ..., default value null, determines hash
        table in which to cache solutions to the deformation equation
      * *note CorrectionMatrix: CorrectionMatrix, => ..., default value "auto",
        determines the first order deformations used in correcting liftings
      * *note DegreeBound: DegreeBound, => ..., default value 0, determines the
        degree limit used to compute the tangent cone of obstruction equations
      * *note HighestOrder: HighestOrder, => ..., default value 20, sets the
        order to which we compute
      * *note PolynomialCheck: PolynomialCheck, => ..., default value true,
        checks if power series solution terminates
      * *note SanityCheck: SanityCheck, => ..., default value true, checks if
        lifting solves deformation equation
      * *note SmartLift: SmartLift, => ..., default value true, chooses lifting
        to avoid obstructions at next order
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value 0, control the verbosity
        of output
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices
      * R, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of matrices

Description
===========

Each element of the sequence (F,R,G,C) is a list of matrices in increasing
powers of the deformation parameter. The input (f,r,g,c) should be a valid
solution to the deformation equation output in the form done by *note
versalDeformation(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix):
versalDeformation_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_cmMatrix_rp,. This function continues
lifting this solution to higher order. All options described for *note
versalDeformation(Matrix): versalDeformation_lpMatrix_rp, may be used to the
same effect.

After each step of lifting, the solution (F,R,G,C) to the deformation equation
is cached. By default, it is stored in (f_0).cache#VersalDeformationResults but
may stored elsewhere by setting the option *note CacheName: CacheName, to
something other than *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,.

This function is especially useful for finding one-parameter families when the
versal family is too complicated to calculate.

We may consider the example of the versal deformation of a degree 12 toric Fano
threefold:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x1,x2,x3,x4,x5,x6,y1,y2,z];                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal {x1*x4-z^2,x2*x5-z^2,x3*x6-z^2,x1*x3-z*x2,x2*x4-z*x3,x3*x5-z*x4,|
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x4*x6-z*x5,x5*x1-z*x6,x6*x2-z*x1,y1*y2-z^2};                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F0=gens I;                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|             1      10                                                       |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (F,R,G,C)=versalDeformation(F0,CT^1(0,F0),CT^2(0,F0),HighestOrder=>2);  |
|Warning: calculation terminated since HighestOrder has been reached.         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We stop the calculation at order 2, since in this case, the solution to the
deformation equation calculated by the lifting algorithm will not be
polynomial. Equations for the tangent cone at the origin of a versal base space
are

+------------------------+
|i5 : T=ring first G;    |
+------------------------+
|i6 : G_0                |
|                        |
|o6 = | t_19t_22        ||
|     | t_20t_23        ||
|     | t_15t_22-t_22^2 ||
|     | t_16t_23-t_23^2 ||
|                        |
|             4      1   |
|o6 : Matrix T  <-- T    |
+------------------------+

This decomposes into four components:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : decompose ideal G_0                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {ideal (t  , t  ), ideal (t  , t  , t   - t  ), ideal (t  , t  , t   -  |
|              23   22           23   19   15    22           22   20   16    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     t  ), ideal (t  , t  , t   - t  , t   - t  )}                           |
|      23           20   19   16    23   15    22                             |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We now find a one-parameter deformation onto the component of highest
dimension:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A=(coefficientRing ring F_0)[s];                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : sublist=apply(gens T,v->(if v==t_19 or v==t_20  then return v=>s;v=>0));|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : f=apply(F,i->sub(i,sublist));                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : r=apply(R,i->sub(i,sublist));                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : g=apply(G,i->sub(i,sublist));                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : c=apply(C,i->sub(i,sublist));                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : (F,R,G,C)=versalDeformation(f,r,g,c);                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : sum F                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o15 = | (y1z+y2z)s+x1x4-z2 (y1z+y2z)s+x2x5-z2 x3x6-z2 x1x3-x2z               |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      (x3y1+x3y2)s+x2x4-x3z x3x5-x4z x4x6-x5z (x6y1+x6y2)s+x1x5-x6z x2x6-x1z |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      y1y2-z2 |                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|              1      10                                                      |
|o15 : Matrix A  <-- A                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note versalDeformation(List,List,List,List):
    versalDeformation_lpList_cmList_cmList_cmList_rp, -- continues calculation
    of  a versal deformation
