versalDeformation(NestedDeformation) -- continues calculation of  a versal deformation
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note versalDeformation: versalDeformation,
  * Usage: 
        E = versalDeformation(D)
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeBound: DegreeBound, => ..., default value 0, determines the
        degree limit used to compute the tangent cone of obstruction equations
      * *note HighestOrder: HighestOrder, => ..., default value 20, sets the
        order to which we compute
      * *note PolynomialCheck: PolynomialCheck, => ..., default value true,
        checks if power series solution terminates
      * *note SanityCheck: SanityCheck, => ..., default value true, checks if
        lifting solves deformation equation
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value 0, control the verbosity
        of output
  * Outputs:
      * E, an instance of the type *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation,

Description
===========

This method iteratively lifts a *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation, D
to higher and higher order.

For example, consider embedded deformations of the fat points in the plane
defined by the square and cube of the homogeneous maximal ideal.  The following
lifts a first order *note NestedDeformation: NestedDeformation, for this pair
to higher order:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y];                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F0Y=basis(3,R);                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|             1      4                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F0X=basis(2,R);                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|             1      3                                                        |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : T1Y=normalMatrix(F0Y);                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|             4      12                                                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T1X=normalMatrix(F0X);                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|             3      6                                                        |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : T2X=CT^2(F0X);                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|             2      1                                                        |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : T2Y=CT^2(F0Y);                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : T2XY=nestedObstruction(F0X,F0Y);                                        |
|                                                                             |
|             4      8                                                        |
|o8 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : D=setupNestedDeformation({F0X,T1X,T2X,F0Y,T1Y,T2Y,T2XY});               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : E=versalDeformation(D,Verbose=>4);                                     |
